---
title: "Pancakes - made to be more diabetic healthy"
description: "simple Pancakes for diabetics"
date: "2026-09-01"
tags: ["sauce", "vegetarian", "make-ahead"]
prepTime: "10 min"
cookTime: "5 min"
totalTime: "15 min"
servings: 5
nutrition:
---

- 1 1/2 cups oat flour
- 1 tsp baking powder
- 1 tsp ground cinnamon
- 1/4 tsp salt
- 2 large eggs
- 2 tsp Splenda
- 3/4 cup unsweetened oat milk, coconut milk, or regular milk
- 1 tbsp melted coconut oil or butter

## Instructions

1. Whisk the oat flour, baking powder, cinnamon, and salt in a bowl.
2. In a separate bowl, beat the eggs and whisk in your chosen milk and melted oil/butter.
3. Combine the wet and dry ingredients. Let the batter rest for 10 minutes so the oat flour can absorb the liquid properly.
4. Cook over medium-low heat on a lightly greased skillet until bubbles form, flip, and cook until golden brown.
5. Top with fresh berries or a dollop of Greek yogurt.
